# this is code to generate the 
# discriminant of 
# 
# x^6+ay^3+y=0 
# y^6+bx^3+x=0
#
# the degree of the resultant of 
# GENERIC polys with support = 
# (supp(f),supp(g),suff(Jac(f,g))) 
# should be 35+45+45=125, and this implies that 
# the degree of the resulting principal 
# A-determinant should be <= 35*2+45+45=160... 
# 
# ...thus it would appear to imply that rr2 (the 
# degree 90 factor below, not the degree 485 factor) 
# is the discriminant I want! 
#
# incidentally, the calculation took 3h22m6.251s 
# on thelonius! 
# 

f:=x^6+a*y^3+y;  
g:=y^6+b*x^3+x;
fx:=diff(f,x); fy:=diff(f,y);
gx:=diff(g,x); gy:=diff(g,y);
j:=simplify(fx*gy-fy*gx);

r1:=resultant(f,j,x);
r2:=resultant(g,j,x); 

rr:=factor(resultant(r1,r2,y));
rr1:=op(1,rr); rr2:=op(2,rr); rr3:=op(3,rr);  





